%% 07 — Delivery timeline by epic
%% Drawn from: gh pr list --state merged (336 PRs into dev or a stack branch,
%%   2026-09-13 to 2026-11-07, the cut-off), each PR's closing issue and its
%%   "epic:" label, else the issue's parent, else the story tag in the title
%%   ([5.x] is infra, as #19, #20 and #599 are labelled). 67 PRs with no epic
%%   anywhere are the last lane; #221's void stack, unlabelled, is under
%%   resolution. Releases are the [Release] PRs into main, named as their
%%   titles name them. #633, which merged main back into dev, is a PR into dev
%%   with no epic, so it is in the last lane; #664 and #666, docs PRs straight
%%   into main, are not drawn.
%%   #19's five PRs, #603 to #607, are in the infra lane; "Production" marks the
%%   days it went live and the two load-test runs in production, from
%%   docs/load-test.md's results table.
%% A bar runs from an epic's first merged PR to its last. It is a span, not
%% continuous work. FE bars are shaded (`active`), BE bars plain.
%% Compact mode shares a row between bars that do not overlap, which would pile
%% the milestone labels onto one row. Mermaid draws a milestone at the middle of
%% its span, and fills a section's rows greedily in order of each span's start,
%% so each milestone is given a span centred on its date (releases 4, 17, 19, 20,
%% 24 and 29 Oct and 1, 4 and 7 Nov) whose start puts labels that would collide
%% on different rows. The span itself is not drawn. "It." is Iteration, as the
%% release PRs' titles name them. Two dates had two release PRs, and the chart
%% names the later one: #597 and #613 on 1 Nov, and #631 and #632, the two steps
%% of one release, on 4 Nov.
%%{init: {"gantt": {"displayMode": "compact", "barHeight": 18, "barGap": 4}, "themeCSS": ".tick text { font-size: 15px; } .sectionTitle { font-size: 15px; } .taskText, .taskTextOutsideRight, .taskTextOutsideLeft { font-size: 14.5px; }"}}%%
